\f2 \cf12 \cb13 Container Orchestration: Managed Kubernetes
\f1\fs32 \cf14 \cb1 \
\pard\pardeftab720\sa320\partightenfactor0
\cf15 \cb3 This lab demonstrates how to deploy a basic NGINX web server on your existing Amazon EKS cluster. We\'92ll create a Deployment, expose it via a LoadBalancer Service, and verify that it\'92s working. Time to see those containers in action\'97cue the confetti!\cb1 \

\fs48 \cf2 \cb3 Prerequisites\cb1 \
\pard\tx220\tx720\pardeftab720\li720\fi-720\sa120\partightenfactor0
\ls1\ilvl0
\fs32 \cf15 \cb3 \kerning1\expnd0\expndtw0 {\listtext	\uc0\u8226 	}\expnd0\expndtw0\kerning0
You have an 
\f3\b Amazon EKS
\f1\b0  cluster up and running.\cb1 \
\pard\tx940\tx1440\pardeftab720\li1440\fi-1440\partightenfactor0
\ls1\ilvl1\cf15 \cb3 \kerning1\expnd0\expndtw0 {\listtext	\uc0\u8226 	}\expnd0\expndtw0\kerning0
If you need to set one up, see the 
\f0 \AppleTypeServices\AppleTypeServicesF65539 \cf16 previous lab on creating an EKS cluster with 
\f1 \AppleTypeServices eksctl\cf15 .\cb1 \
\pard\tx220\tx720\pardeftab720\li720\fi-720\partightenfactor0
\ls1\ilvl0
\f3\b \cf15 \cb3 \kerning1\expnd0\expndtw0 {\listtext	\uc0\u8226 	}\expnd0\expndtw0\kerning0
kubectl
\f1\b0  is configured to point to your EKS cluster.\cb1 \
\pard\tx940\tx1440\pardeftab720\li1440\fi-1440\partightenfactor0
\ls1\ilvl1\cf15 \cb3 \kerning1\expnd0\expndtw0 {\listtext	\uc0\u8226 	}\expnd0\expndtw0\kerning0
Test with: 
\f4 kubectl get nodes
\f1 \cb1 \
\pard\pardeftab720\sa320\partightenfactor0

\fs48 \cf2 \cb3 Step 1: Create a Deployment\cb1 \
\pard\tx220\tx720\pardeftab720\li720\fi-720\sa320\partightenfactor0
\ls2\ilvl0
\f3\b\fs32 \cf15 \cb3 \kerning1\expnd0\expndtw0 {\listtext	1	}\expnd0\expndtw0\kerning0
Create
\f1\b0  a Kubernetes Deployment for NGINX:\cb1 \uc0\u8232 
\fs28 \cf17 \cb3 kubectl\cf18  create deployment nginx-deployment\cf19  --image=nginx:latest\cf15 \cb1 \uc0\u8232 
\f4\fs32 \uc0\u8232 
\f1 \uc0\u8232 
\f0\fs24 \AppleTypeServices\AppleTypeServicesF65539 \uc0\u8232 \AppleTypeServices\AppleTypeServicesF65539 \cb3 Copy\AppleTypeServices\AppleTypeServicesF65539 \cb1 \uc0\u8232 \AppleTypeServices\AppleTypeServicesF65539 \cf20 \uc0\u8232 \cb21 Explain\cb1 \uc0\u8232 
\f1\fs32 \AppleTypeServices \cf15 \cb3 \uc0\u8232 \cb1 \uc0\u8232 \u8232 \cb3 This command does the following:\cb1 \
\pard\tx940\tx1440\pardeftab720\li1440\fi-1440\partightenfactor0
\ls2\ilvl1\cf15 \cb3 \kerning1\expnd0\expndtw0 {\listtext	\uc0\u8226 	}\expnd0\expndtw0\kerning0
Pulls the 
\f4 nginx:latest\cb1 \uc0\u8232 
\f1 \cb3 Docker image from Docker Hub. Spins up a Deployment named 
\f4 nginx-deployment\cb1 \uc0\u8232 
\f1 \cb3 , which includes a ReplicaSet and one Pod by default (unless specified otherwise).\cb1 \
\pard\tx220\tx720\pardeftab720\li720\fi-720\sa320\partightenfactor0
\ls2\ilvl0
\f3\b \cf15 \cb3 \kerning1\expnd0\expndtw0 {\listtext	2	}\expnd0\expndtw0\kerning0
Verify
\f1\b0  the Deployment:\cb1 \uc0\u8232 
\fs28 \cf17 \cb3 kubectl\cf18  get deployments\cf15 \cb1 \uc0\u8232 
\f4\fs32 \uc0\u8232 
\f1 \uc0\u8232 
\f0\fs24 \AppleTypeServices\AppleTypeServicesF65539 \uc0\u8232 \AppleTypeServices\AppleTypeServicesF65539 \cb3 Copy\AppleTypeServices\AppleTypeServicesF65539 \cb1 \uc0\u8232 \AppleTypeServices\AppleTypeServicesF65539 \cf20 \uc0\u8232 \cb21 Explain\cb1 \uc0\u8232 
\f1\fs32 \AppleTypeServices \cf15 \cb3 \uc0\u8232 \cb1 \uc0\u8232 \u8232 \cb3 You should see output similar to:\cb1 \uc0\u8232 
\f4 \cb22 NAME                READY   UP-TO-DATE   AVAILABLE   AGE\
\pard\tx220\tx720\pardeftab720\li720\fi-720\partightenfactor0
\ls2\ilvl0\cf15 \kerning1\expnd0\expndtw0 {\listtext	3	}\expnd0\expndtw0\kerning0
nginx-deployment    1/1     1            1           10s\
\ls2\ilvl0\kerning1\expnd0\expndtw0 {\listtext	4	}\expnd0\expndtw0\kerning0
\uc0\u8232 
\f1 \cb3 And check the Pods:\cb1 \uc0\u8232 
\fs28 \cf17 \cb3 kubectl\cf18  get pods\cf15 \cb1 \uc0\u8232 
\f4\fs32 \uc0\u8232 
\f1 \uc0\u8232 
\f0\fs24 \AppleTypeServices\AppleTypeServicesF65539 \uc0\u8232 \AppleTypeServices\AppleTypeServicesF65539 \cb3 Copy\AppleTypeServices\AppleTypeServicesF65539 \cb1 \uc0\u8232 \AppleTypeServices\AppleTypeServicesF65539 \cf20 \uc0\u8232 \cb21 Explain\cb1 \uc0\u8232 
\f1\fs32 \AppleTypeServices \cf15 \cb3 \uc0\u8232 \cb1 \uc0\u8232 \u8232 \cb3 You\'92ll see a Pod named something like 
\f4 nginx-deployment-xxxxxxx-xxxxx
\f1  in the 
\f4 Running
\f1  state.\cf14 \cb1 \
\pard\pardeftab720\sa320\partightenfactor0

\fs48 \cf2 \cb3 Step 2: Expose the Deployment\cb1 \

\fs32 \cf15 \cb3 Next, we\'92ll expose the NGINX Pods externally so we can access them via a load balancer.\cb1 \
\pard\tx220\tx720\pardeftab720\li720\fi-720\sa320\partightenfactor0
\ls3\ilvl0
\f3\b \cf15 \cb3 \kerning1\expnd0\expndtw0 {\listtext	1	}\expnd0\expndtw0\kerning0
Create
\f1\b0  a Service of type 
\f3\b LoadBalancer
\f1\b0 :\cb1 \uc0\u8232 
\fs28 \cf17 \cb3 kubectl\cf18  expose deployment nginx-deployment\cf19  \\\cf15 \
\pard\tx220\tx720\pardeftab720\li720\fi-720\partightenfactor0
\ls3\ilvl0\cf19 \kerning1\expnd0\expndtw0 {\listtext	2	}\expnd0\expndtw0\kerning0
  --type=LoadBalancer \\\cf15 \
\ls3\ilvl0\cf19 \kerning1\expnd0\expndtw0 {\listtext	3	}\expnd0\expndtw0\kerning0
  --port=80 \\\cf15 \
\ls3\ilvl0\cf19 \kerning1\expnd0\expndtw0 {\listtext	4	}\expnd0\expndtw0\kerning0
  --name=nginx-service\cf15 \cb1 \uc0\u8232 
\f4\fs32 \uc0\u8232 
\f1 \uc0\u8232 
\f0\fs24 \AppleTypeServices\AppleTypeServicesF65539 \uc0\u8232 \AppleTypeServices\AppleTypeServicesF65539 \cb3 Copy\AppleTypeServices\AppleTypeServicesF65539 \cb1 \uc0\u8232 \AppleTypeServices\AppleTypeServicesF65539 \cf20 \uc0\u8232 \cb21 Explain\cb1 \uc0\u8232 
\f1\fs32 \AppleTypeServices \cf15 \cb3 \uc0\u8232 \cb1 \uc0\u8232 \
\pard\tx940\tx1440\pardeftab720\li1440\fi-1440\partightenfactor0
\ls3\ilvl1
\f4 \cf15 \cb3 \kerning1\expnd0\expndtw0 {\listtext	\uc0\u8226 	}\expnd0\expndtw0\kerning0
--type=LoadBalancer\cb1 \uc0\u8232 
\f1 \cb3 : Tells Kubernetes to provision an AWS Elastic Load Balancer (ELB). 
\f4 --port=80\cb1 \uc0\u8232 
\f1 \cb3 : The service will listen on port 80. 
\f4 --name=nginx-service\cb1 \uc0\u8232 
\f1 \cb3 : Names the Service resource.\cb1 \
\pard\tx220\tx720\pardeftab720\li720\fi-720\sa320\partightenfactor0
\ls3\ilvl0
\f3\b \cf15 \cb3 \kerning1\expnd0\expndtw0 {\listtext	5	}\expnd0\expndtw0\kerning0
Check
\f1\b0  the Service:\cb1 \uc0\u8232 
\fs28 \cf17 \cb3 kubectl\cf18  get svc nginx-service\cf15 \cb1 \uc0\u8232 
\f4\fs32 \uc0\u8232 
\f1 \uc0\u8232 
\f0\fs24 \AppleTypeServices\AppleTypeServicesF65539 \uc0\u8232 \AppleTypeServices\AppleTypeServicesF65539 \cb3 Copy\AppleTypeServices\AppleTypeServicesF65539 \cb1 \uc0\u8232 \AppleTypeServices\AppleTypeServicesF65539 \cf20 \uc0\u8232 \cb21 Explain\cb1 \uc0\u8232 
\f1\fs32 \AppleTypeServices \cf15 \cb3 \uc0\u8232 \cb1 \uc0\u8232 \u8232 \cb3 Initially, the EXTERNAL-IP column may show 
\f4 <pending>
\f1 . After a minute or two, AWS will provision a load balancer, and the EXTERNAL-IP field will update to a DNS name or IP address.\cf14 \cb1 \
\pard\pardeftab720\sa320\partightenfactor0

\fs48 \cf2 \cb3 Step 3: Test the Application\cb1 \
\pard\tx220\tx720\pardeftab720\li720\fi-720\sa320\partightenfactor0
\ls4\ilvl0
\f3\b\fs32 \cf15 \cb3 \kerning1\expnd0\expndtw0 {\listtext	1	}\expnd0\expndtw0\kerning0
Wait
\f1\b0  for the Service to be ready. Once it shows a valid 
\f3\b EXTERNAL-IP
\f1\b0 , note that value.\cb1 \uc0\u8232 
\f3\b \cb3 Access
\f1\b0  the app in your browser or via curl:\cb1 \uc0\u8232 
\fs28 \cf17 \cb3 curl\cf18  http://\cf23 <\cf18 EXTERNAL-I\cf24 P\cf23 >\cf15 \cb1 \uc0\u8232 
\f4\fs32 \uc0\u8232 
\f1 \uc0\u8232 
\f0\fs24 \AppleTypeServices\AppleTypeServicesF65539 \uc0\u8232 \AppleTypeServices\AppleTypeServicesF65539 \cb3 Copy\AppleTypeServices\AppleTypeServicesF65539 \cb1 \uc0\u8232 \AppleTypeServices\AppleTypeServicesF65539 \cf20 \uc0\u8232 \cb21 Explain\cb1 \uc0\u8232 
\f1\fs32 \AppleTypeServices \cf15 \cb3 \uc0\u8232 \cb1 \uc0\u8232 \u8232 \cb3 You should see the 
\f3\b default NGINX welcome page
\f1\b0 . If so, 
\f5\i confetti time!
\f1\i0  You\'92ve just deployed a simple NGINX web server on EKS.\cb1 \uc0\u8232 
\f3\b \cb3 (Optional)
\f1\b0  Scale the Deployment if you want more replicas:\cb1 \uc0\u8232 
\fs28 \cf17 \cb3 kubectl\cf18  scale deployment nginx-deployment\cf19  --replicas=3\cf15 \cb1 \uc0\u8232 
\f4\fs32 \uc0\u8232 
\f1 \uc0\u8232 
\f0\fs24 \AppleTypeServices\AppleTypeServicesF65539 \uc0\u8232 \AppleTypeServices\AppleTypeServicesF65539 \cb3 Copy\AppleTypeServices\AppleTypeServicesF65539 \cb1 \uc0\u8232 \AppleTypeServices\AppleTypeServicesF65539 \cf20 \uc0\u8232 \cb21 Explain\cb1 \uc0\u8232 
\f1\fs32 \AppleTypeServices \cf15 \cb3 \uc0\u8232 \cb1 \uc0\u8232 \u8232 \cb3 Then verify:\cb1 \uc0\u8232 
\fs28 \cf17 \cb3 kubectl\cf18  get pods\cf15 \cb1 \uc0\u8232 
\f4\fs32 \uc0\u8232 
\f1 \uc0\u8232 
\f0\fs24 \AppleTypeServices\AppleTypeServicesF65539 \uc0\u8232 \AppleTypeServices\AppleTypeServicesF65539 \cb3 Copy\AppleTypeServices\AppleTypeServicesF65539 \cb1 \uc0\u8232 \AppleTypeServices\AppleTypeServicesF65539 \cf20 \uc0\u8232 \cb21 Explain\cb1 \uc0\u8232 
\f1\fs32 \AppleTypeServices \cf15 \cb3 \uc0\u8232 \cb1 \uc0\u8232 \u8232 \cb3 You\'92ll see 3 Pods running. The Service load balancer will automatically distribute traffic among them.\cf14 \cb1 \
\pard\pardeftab720\sa320\partightenfactor0

\fs48 \cf2 \cb3 Step 4: Cleanup (Optional)\cb1 \

\fs32 \cf15 \cb3 If you no longer need the NGINX app, remove it to save costs and keep your cluster tidy:\cb1 \
\pard\pardeftab720\partightenfactor0

\fs28 \cf17 \cb3 kubectl\cf18  delete service nginx-service\cf14 \
\cf17 kubectl\cf18  delete deployment nginx-deployment\cf14 \cb1 \
\pard\pardeftab720\qc\partightenfactor0

\f2\fs24 \cf15 \
\cb3 Copy\cb1 \
\cf20 \
\cb21 Explain\cb1 \
\pard\pardeftab720\sa320\partightenfactor0

\f1\fs32 \cf15 \cb3 Kubernetes will terminate the Pods, remove the Service, and AWS will delete the associated load balancer.\cb1 \

\fs48 \cf2 \cb3 Summary\cb1 \
\pard\tx220\tx720\pardeftab720\li720\fi-720\sa120\partightenfactor0
\ls5\ilvl0
\f3\b\fs32 \cf15 \cb3 \kerning1\expnd0\expndtw0 {\listtext	\uc0\u8226 	}\expnd0\expndtw0\kerning0
Deployment
\f1\b0 : We created a Deployment running the official NGINX Docker image.\cb1 \
